        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: To Be or Not to Be (1983 film)\n- People: Mel Brooks, Alan Johnson, Charles Durning\n- Topics: American war comedy films, acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- Mel Brooks, born Melvin Kaminsky on June 28, 1926, is an American actor, writer, producer, director, comedian, and composer.\n- Charles Durning's best-known roles included The Sting (1973) and Dog Day Afternoon (1975).\n- Charles Durning's best-known comedy roles included The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas (1982), Tootsie (1982), and To Be or Not to Be (1983).\n- To Be or Not to Be is a 1983 American war comedy film directed by Alan Johnson and produced by Mel Brooks.",
